1 	This folder is for the official plots webpage on t2k.org.
2 	
3 	After collecting all the desired .png, .eps and .pdf files, run the following two commands:
4 	
5 	1) ./mk_official_plots.sh tn108_plots.zip > index.html
6 	2) ./mk_official_plots_zip.sh tn108_plots
7 	
8 	Then:
9 	
10 	3) create a new folder on t2k.org (Plone), for example, "TN-108 Official Plots" here: http://www.t2k.org/comm/pubboard/review/2012a/NIWG
11 	4) Click the "Contents" tab, then the "Import" button
12 	5) Select the .zip file you created in #2 and click "Import"
13 	
14 	This should extract everything in the Plone folder, including the index.html webpage which should appear as:
15 	
16 	http://www.t2k.org/comm/pubboard/review/2012a/NIWG/tn108-plots/
17 	
18 	Note that the descriptions need to be modified manually on Plone.
19 	
20 	------------------------------------------
21 	
22 	Some other useful tools here which should be self-explanatory:
23 	
24 	convert_eps_to_png.sh
25 	convert_pdf_to_eps_to_png.sh
26 	getpdfs.sh

Just run the following (add more plots in get_eps.sh):



#do the old (sinsq2theta) plots
rm -r *eps *pdf *png index.html tn141_official_plots*
./get_eps.sh
./convert_eps_to_png_and_pdf.sh
./mk_official_plots.sh tn141_official_plots > index.html
cp index_edit.html index.html
./mk_official_plots_zip.sh tn141_official_plots


#do the sinsqtheta plots
rm -r *eps *pdf *png index.html tn141_official_plots*
./get_eps_sinsqtheta.sh
./convert_eps_to_png_and_pdf.sh
./mk_official_plots.sh tn141_official_plots > index.html
cp index_edit_new.html index.html
./mk_official_plots_zip.sh tn141_official_plots




index_edit.html is a version of index.html, but with the captions included. Save time by editing this, when new plots are added.

